# sau-web frontend env (Vite) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to `sau_web/frontend/.env` (or `.env.local`) and edit;
# values flow into the React tree via `import.meta.env.<KEY>` and must
# be prefixed `VITE_` to be exposed in the browser bundle. Variables
# without the `VITE_` prefix stay server-only and are NOT readable from
# the front-end.
#
# The backend Python process reads the REPO-ROOT `.env` (with `SAU_*`
# keys for DB / SMTP / CORS / etc.) — that's a DIFFERENT file. Do NOT
# put frontend `VITE_*` keys in the repo root, and do NOT put `SAU_*`
# keys here. The two layers have independent env contracts.
#
# Vite auto-loads `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.development`, and
# `.env.production` from this directory. `.env.local` is gitignored
# and is the standard path for per-developer overrides.

# ── Brand mark ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Visitor-facing brand text. Renders in:
#   • AppShell mobile top-header (`<header>` on `≤768 px`)
#   • AppShell desktop sidebar brand lockup (expanded mode only)
#   • AppShell desktop top-header mono breadcrumb
# Falls back to `sau` when unset.
# VITE_APP_NAME=sau

# ── Build SHA ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Short or full git SHA. Renders as `build <sha-7chars>` in:
#   • AppShell sidebar brand lockup (expanded mode only)
#   • AppShell desktop top-header mono breadcrumb
# Falls back to `dev` when unset so `pnpm dev` shows `build dev`.
# VITE_GIT_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
